        "original_id": "ee6a57dc-605d-5d5a-a2d0-854824298aed",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Daniel Inouye\n- Organizations: United States Senate, Democratic Party\n- Places: Hawaii, United States\n- Events: 1992 United States Senate election in Hawaii\n- Roles: United States Senator, President pro tempore of the United States Senate\n\nFacts:\n- Daniel Inouye was a United States Senator from Hawaii from 1963 to 2012.\n- Daniel Inouye was a member of the Democratic Party.\n- In the 1992 United States Senate election in Hawaii, incumbent Democratic U.S. Senator Daniel Inouye won re-election to a sixth term.\n- From 2010 until his death in 2012, Daniel Inouye served as President pro tempore of the United States Senate.\n- Daniel Inouye became the highest-ranking Japanese American politician in U.S. history through his service as President pro tempore of the United States Senate.",
